  "rationale": "The structural obligations of `requirements.sdk.graph.context-tools.list_sources.fn` are met.\n\n- **Method signature.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[list]` is declared as `pub async fn list(&self, scope: &SourceScope) -> Result<Vec<PathBuf>, SourceError>`. This matches the required signature exactly. It sits in `impl Sources`, and the types `Sources`, `SourceScope` (struct with a `prefix`) and `SourceError` (enum with `Io` and `Invalid`) all exist in the same file.\n- **Delegation.** `Sources::list` delegates to `self.analysis.provider.list(scope)` and maps each returned `ResourceId` to a `PathBuf` from its `location`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#trait[SourceProvider]/fn[list]` declares the provider-side listing that backs it, taking the same `&SourceScope`. `LocalSources` implements it.\n- **Tool exposure.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<'_, P, F, D::NodeId, D::EdgeLabel>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` exposes a `list_sources` tool definition that takes an optional `prefix`. In the same impl, `fn[dispatch]` routes the `list_sources` command to `provider.list(&scope)`. The project-directory scoping is enforced by the local provider and is a behavioral matter outside this structural check.\n\nI found no structural gap and no conflicting element. There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments, and none are needed.",
